WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.002
Materialized-view freshness is easiest to understand as a timeline.

00:00:05.002 --> 00:00:10.637
The snapshot is built. Later, a new base-table row arrives.

00:00:10.637 --> 00:00:16.947
The standard base query can see it immediately, but the materialized view does not.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:18.757
After a refresh, the stored snapshot catches up.

00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:22.642
That delay must be documented for users.

00:00:22.642 --> 00:00:28.807
A materialized view stores the query result physically, trading freshness for faster reads.

00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:35.212
That makes refresh policy part of the data contract.

00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:40.722
A dashboard should know whether the snapshot is five minutes old or one day old.

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:45.891
Indexes can improve access, and concurrent refresh has additional requirements.
